.TH AVR\-SERVICE\-TOKEN\-LIST 1 "" "avr" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-service-token-list \- List the organization's service tokens, soonest expiry first.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr service-token list
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
List the organization's service tokens, soonest expiry first.
.PP
Lists live, expired and revoked tokens; tokens that never expire come last. A live token whose requests are refused all the same, for example while its group is suspended, shows as blocked with the reason.
.PP
--group takes a group ID or a group's path as `avr group list` shows it, such as Acme/Platform/CI. The end of a path, such as Platform/CI or a group name like CI, works when it selects only one group.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr service-token list
    avr service-token list --status live --group Platform/CI
    avr service-token list --json id,name,expires_at
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    blocked_by, created_at, created_by, expires_at, expiring_soon, grants,
    grants_version, group_id, id, last_used_at, name, organization_id,
    previous_valid_until, revoked_at, revoked_reason, rotated_at,
    rotation_version, status
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR \fITEXT\fR
Only the tokens this group owns, by group name, path or ID (grp-xxx).
.TP
\fB\-\-status\fR \fICHOICE\fR
Only tokens with this status. (choices: live, expired, revoked)
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-limit\fR \fIINTEGER RANGE\fR
Max tokens to return. (default: 50)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
